FILE final529r20_20260930/crime_width_probe.r20.py
480:     REDIRECTS the pc (revP sw pc, revP sd pc), and at CONTROL the arm's effects (sw08 halts, sw08 msg ctl at 4 bytes;
481:     acc ctl sd at 8).  [This bullet said "no round trip there can observe whether the store was accepted" as though
482:     nothing could, and it was wrong twice: the window redirect (measured by the Opus seat, G4) and the 8-byte CONTROL
483:     write, which no row carried until repair 12 -- closing pass 6.]  The 4R-high cell at +0x00 is carried by `rev pc
484:     ctl' (its redirect needs the access ACCEPTED), not by `devsig hi', whose 0 a refused read also returns.
485:   * `odata = idata' in the decline arm: EQUIVALENT by construction -- `idata' is set only under MEM_WRITE and `odata' is
486:     consumed only under MEM_READ (measured 141/141 on the 141-row test by the Opus seat, closing pass 6).  `cpu->is_32bit' (the REV arm's
487:     pc-pointer refresh) holds one value per machine, like the configuration lvalues above.  Accepted-side address bits 7
488:     and 8: the mid session's accepted sd +0x1f8 carries both, before and between its refusals (a latch keyed on them is
489:     killed -- kimi-k3's C3, 139/141 on the 141-row test); an ACCEPT arm keyed on them is the unrowed-slot class above.
490:   * ACCEPTS has 46 ENTRIES, not 46 kinds: the 40-cell pre-set/re-arm floor, the two ENDIANESS strengthenings, and four
491:     positional repeats of default-arm kinds (`sw/lw 0x04' repeat 0x34's low lane; `sd/ld 0x278' repeat 0x40's 8-byte
492:     kinds, and are the prologue's only accepted access with address bit 9 set -- an unrecorded strengthening until
493:     repair 12; kimi CLI, closing pass 6).
494:   * a decline answering a selection of the register's bytes at CRIME_REV, CRIME_CONTROL or CRIME_TIME CONFINED to
495:     bytes the model holds at 0 there -- REV = 0x11: bytes 1-7; CONTROL = 0x100: byte 0 and bytes 2-7; TIME: the 4-byte
496:     half above the low word -- is EQUIVALENT (the prelude rewrites REV and CONTROL on every access) -- at TIME only
497:     WHILE ITS UPPER WORD IS ZERO: the clock update truncates TIME to 32 bits only inside `if (to_add >= 1)', and an
498:     accepted 8-byte or upper-half write can fill the upper word, so a nonzero upper word survives a zero-delta update
499:     (a source reading, GPT-6 Astra's r17 audit; this said "TIME is kept to 32 bits" unconditionally, and no row
500:     seeds TIME's upper word).  [Corrected 2026-09-14 from closing pass 5 (glm): this read "the ADDRESSED lanes (bytes 0-1 at a label)",
501:     which at REV and CONTROL include a NONZERO byte -- item 9's v0 rows exist to catch exactly that selection.]  At
502:     INTSTAT, INTMASK and DOG every byte is seeded nonzero, so any selection that reaches the bytes a refused lb/lh
503:     returns shows (Opus, second closing pass; glm, third) -- one confined above them, `& 0xffff0000', is item 9's
504:     disclosed equivalent (the qualifier: GPT-6 Astra's r17 audit; this said "any selection shows").
505:   * a latch keyed on a JOINT predicate (e.g. only 2-byte refusals at CRIME_TIME), or on one unnamed offset other than the
506:     default-arm cells the latch rows refuse at: clause (e), the single-axis generating set being the floor.
507:   * (closing pass 5; the Opus seat measured each at 141/141 on the 141-row test; the flagship ruling graded each clause
508:     (e)) a latch re-armed or pre-set by a CONTROL write's ENDIANESS bit (0x100) -- the arm clears it unconditionally and
