1825: > > struct LAYOUT, because which cell an out-of-bounds index lands on is itself a layout fact.**
1826: >
1827: > *So the two cautions are not a contrast between a weak row and a strong one. Both rows are
1828: > layout-dependent; the anchored one is additionally decode-absolute. Stating it as a contrast
1829: > made the anchor rule sound like it bought more than it does -- in the carrier, where future
1830: > rounds apply it.*
1831: > And **translations beyond the measured ones are not covered by having measured +/-1**: a
1832: > derivation says `+2` escapes both the distinctness rows and that round's anchored row. A
1833: > contract must claim the translations it MEASURED and disclose the rest.
1834: 
1835: > ### *** THE LATE-DISSENT RULE -- adopted 2026-08-25, after a panel stage fired AFTER a round
1836: > ### had committed returned 4-2 AGAINST the shipped fix. ***
1837: >
1838: > `#463` closed with its research stage at 3 of 9. An exemption was offered to the owner and
1839: > **DECLINED in favour of firing the missing seats** -- and the filled stage dissented on code
1840: > that had already shipped. There was no rule for that, so:
1841: >
1842: > > **A panel stage fired after a round closes adjudicates like any other finding. Closure
1843: > > changes the LICENSE, never the truth-value.** Three dispositions, exhaustive:
1844: > >
1845: > > 1. **WRONG RECORD -> L4, correct in place.** Closure is no shield for false prose.
1846: > > 2. **MEASURED FALSE PASS** against the shipped detector's floor, contract or obligations
1847: > >    -> L2/L3 per the existing rules, in a follow-up commit.
1848: > > 3. **EVERYTHING ELSE, design dissents included -> FILES AS A NEW QUEUE ITEM**, carrying the
1849: > >    dissent VERBATIM as provenance and ranked by severity like any filed item. The closed
1850: > >    round's record gains one line naming the dissent and where it went, **so a future reader
1851: > >    never sees false unanimity.**
1852: > >
1853: > > **Never amend shipped code under a closed round's number**, and never let "the round is
1854: > > closed" reduce a dissent to a footnote no queue item carries.
1855: >
1856: > **THE DISCRIMINATOR for whether a filed dissent earns a round is the universal one: CAN IT
1857: > STATE A MEASURABLE CONSEQUENCE?** `#463b` could -- a `+2` translation predicted to sweep the
1858: > shipped detector clean, and an added-`case` scenario that passes the de-escalation membership
1859: > test. A design dissent that can name no measurement files as documented-only.
